==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*10 [[Bore]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 0.33 seconds<sup>10f</sup>.
*9 [[The Face|Faces]] spawn, delay 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Take it slow! The enemy limit is 10, so each enemy slain will make room for one Bore to spawn; ergo, you only have to fight one at a time provided you never kill The Faces. Of course, slow as they may be, The Faces effectively create a unstoppable wall that obliterates any cat with less range than them, so you can't waste too much time or they'll eventually reach the [[Cat Base]]. After the first three or four Bores, you should move onto fighting two at a time. To sum it up, play too aggressively and you'll face more Bores than you can handle, play too conservatively and The Faces will corner you.

Since the Bores are the main problem, you should dedicate your lineup to [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|Anti-Reds]]. The classic [[Seasons of Love (Combo)|Seasons of Love]] + [[Three Kings (Combo)|Three Kings]] + [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Whales]] is effective as always, especially with their single-target attacks and short range (they won't kill more than one Face at a time), while [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can be used as an "emergency button" to deal massive damage against two or more Bores towards the end. [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|Holy Valkyrie Cat]] is a decent option as well.

Using a Rich Cat will make the beginning a lot smoother, as that Rain D. can take an eternity to kill.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Cat]] and [[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]] are able to trivialize crowd-controlling the Bores, eliminating the only threat in the level.
*[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Kubilan Paslan]] is able to cheese this stage by knocking back both Bores & Faces while standing safely away from them.
*Huge-DPS units like [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]], [[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)|Bunny & Canard]], and [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]] trivialize the enemies in this stage.

